  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Displaced Populations and Host Communities Affected by Security Crises and Climate-Related Disasters in Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Central Emergency Response Fund allocation, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is leading the Groupe de Travail Abris et Biens Non Alimentaires, alongside the Minist&#xE8;re de l&apos;Action humanitaire et de la gestion des catastrophes, to provide humanitarian assistance to 3,111 households, comprising 21,779 individuals, including displaced persons, refugees and vulnerable community members in the Diffa region of Niger. This project focuses on the communes of Ch&#xE9;timari and Diffa, as well as parts of the Tillab&#xE9;ri region, including Banibangou and Ouallam. The assistance provided takes the form of emergency shelters (temporary and urgent), improved emergency shelters (durable and long-term), non-food items, and water, hygiene, and sanitation services. These measures contribute to the alleviation of the precarious living conditions faced by these displaced populations and improve their dignity.</narrative>
  </description>
